                    summary = "When managing urticaria medications, safety and consistency are key:\n\n• Avoid NSAID Triggers: Up to 30% of chronic urticaria patients experience severe flare-ups when taking NSAIDs (like Ibuprofen or Aspirin). Use Acetaminophen (Paracetamol) for pain relief instead.\n• Daily Compliance: Antihistamines work best when taken consistently every day to maintain a stable blockade on receptors. Skipping doses allows histamine to bind, triggering flares that are harder to bring back under control.\n• Professional Supervision: Never self-escalate dosages of antihistamines, steroids, or immunosuppressants without direct physician guidance and laboratory monitoring."
