                    summary = "Hormonal fluctuations can significantly influence the severity of urticaria, particularly in females. Estrogen is known to stimulate mast cell degranulation, while progesterone generally acts as a mast cell stabilizer. Rapid drops in progesterone and rises in estrogen prior to menstruation (during the luteal phase) can lower the hives threshold, leading to premenstrual flares. In rare cases, a patient may develop Autoimmune Progesterone Dermatitis (APD), where the immune system reacts directly to progesterone surges."
